userStories.description:
Telegram channel handles the pause/resume lifecycle. (a) Outbound (internal/channels/telegram outbound or invocation_builder): when streaming reports tool_start for ask_user, format and send the question — with options as '❓ {question}

1. {opt_a}
2. {opt_b}
3. {opt_c}

(reply with number, or text for free input)'; without options as '❓ {question}

(reply with text)'. (b) Inbound (internal/channels/telegram inbound or invocation_builder): on each new user message, check chat.Hub for the current thread's run state. If run.Status == 'waiting_for_user' and PendingAskUserCall returns a pending tool_call: parse the user reply — numeric N (1..len(options)) → select options[N-1] as content; numeric out-of-range or 0 → send synthetic reject 'please reply with 1..N or free text' (does NOT consume the pending question); else (non-numeric) → use raw text as content. (c) Inject a tool_result message with {tool_call_id: pending.toolCallID, name: 'ask_user', content: <selected or free-text>} into the next agent loop invocation (NOT a new inbound message — the inbound is consumed by the resume, no separate user_message turn). (d) Run resumes: next loop call sees the resolved tool_call, status returns to running, LLM proceeds. (e) Tests: numbered reply selects correct option; free-text passes through; out-of-range rejected with synthetic message; multi-option round-trip end-to-end; verify run.Status transitions waiting → running.
